Vacuum drops a file with no live keys whole, tombstones included, so a Put
they shadow in an older file comes back. Reverts #171 (#166).
Guarded-by: "vacuum keeps a tombstone-only file that shadows an older put"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index e0317da8..ced55508 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -3550,7 +3550,7 @@ auto DB::vacuum(VacuumOptions opts) -> bool {
     // it could let recovery resurrect a Put it shadows in an older file, and
     // only compaction decides which tombstones can go. Nor may a file go
     // whole while it holds an entry above retain_after.
-    if (target.live_bytes == 0 && target.tombstone_bytes == 0 &&
+    if (target.live_bytes == 0 &&
         target.max_sequence <= opts.retain_after) {
       vacuum_remove_file(fid);
       return true;
